import Reflection.Types

/-!
# Pinned vocabulary for the theory-Qtsl row decoder (revision event 5.1)

The decoder's analogue of `Reflection.Vocab`, one stratum up: a sealed
QTSL-stratum artifact references the baked theory pair's declarations
through (dependency, counter) element references into the minted
closure revisions, and this module carries the pins those references
resolve against — the PRIMARY pair: the two revision content hashes
of revision event 5.1 (`theories/pins/baked_v1_pins.txt`), with the
**fragment pin table** mapping declaration names of the S1 fragment
to their op counters in BOTH closures.  (A frozen legacy pair at
revision event 4 briefly rode beside the primary — installed at the
e5.1 re-pin to keep the first real-byte warrant receipt accepted,
retired in the same motion as that unit's e5.1 re-emission: the
receipt's sealed dep bytes are the primary chid now, so the primary
pair is also where the chid VALUES get their in-tree byte-literal
witness.  The lane pattern remains available should a sealed
artifact ever need a superseded revision resolvable again — the
store is append-only and the provider's `reprovocab::baked` roster
keeps every event's chid constants.)

Derivation posture (the provider's `reprovocab::baked` DepView
architecture, one prover over): the pins are the chids; the counters
are DERIVED from the minted revision bodies — generated by
`crates/qtsl-geolog-provider/examples/dump_baked_vocab.rs`, which routes through the engine's own meta-schema loader on
the embedded chain containers, never transcribed by hand.  The full
2719-row event-5.1 dump is retained as an audit artifact, as is the
event-4 column's dump; the provider's primary pair is
`BAKED_PRIMARY_EVENT = 6` (= revision event 5.1, the transport lift),
verified at generation time.  Measured fact the table's shape records: **sort counters
coincide between the closures, fun counters do not** (`dc` re-derives
with a uniform shift on this fragment, but the table carries both
columns explicitly — offset arithmetic is exactly the hand-maintenance
this posture forbids).

Fragment discipline: this table is the S1 fragment plus the
certificate-stratum names needed for *named* refusals near it, plus
(night 2) the petri-core/BL-leaf vocabulary of the real emitted
warrant unit — the real-byte round-trip's scan surface.  A
reference outside the table refuses at scan time with its
(dependency, counter) witness (`schema_ref_unpinned`); widening the
table is the class-stratum campaign's per-row extension surface.
-/

namespace SuFunctor

